{"id": "077e5d6a-c480-49a2-9fc3-41a5a58721b5", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I realize serverSideEncryptionConfiguration applies to fully managed knowledge bases, not VECTOR type ones—its absence doesn't mean the KB is unencrypted, since Bedrock encrypts by default with an AWS-owned key. For vector KBs backed by OpenSearch Serverless, encryption at rest is actually governed by the OSS collection's own encryption security policy.

So the verdict shouldn't be "unencrypted" — at most it's "not applicable" or a pass with default AWS-owned-key encryption, unless the check specifically requires a customer-managed key. I should hedge since I can't fully confirm the field's behavior for VECTOR-type KBs versus managed ones, but I'll answer concisely with that caveat in mind.

"}]}
